  {
    "episode_id": 75275,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75275.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Good afternoon. This is Ricardo with the code seven podcast network and this is going to be episode 117 of within the trenches. Now a lot has happened in the past few weeks as I keep saying also before I forget this episode is sponsored by indigital leader and next gen core services. I posted a video. yesterday, actually late last night, or the night before. See, my days are all mixed up now because there's so much stuff that's been going on. But I posted this video that gives an update on the hashtag, I am nine on one movement. And within that video and that update, it gives the numbers, the numbers from all the people that have been posting and sharing the stories, this whole reclassification thing has really started to ramp up. And there's only five days left for the public comments. So we got to keep pushing with this, keep it trending on Twitter and on Facebook. And these stories are They're important. They need to be out there. And that's what's going on with this movement. So in that video, I will put a link on the post for this episode so that you can check that out. Make sure to watch it, share it. There's also a part in there where I address this change.org petition that's been started in the name of the hashtag IAM901 movement. Unfortunately, that petition is not affiliated with the movement that I started. Although I appreciate the effort and the help, it kind of goes against what we're trying to do. What we wanted to do was to share the stories of dispatchers, to show how we differ from commercial dispatchers and clerical workers. This is an effort to assist both APCO and NINA. And by starting a petition, in my opinion, if we were to do that, that only looks as if, you know, we're going up against them and we're not trying to do that. We're trying to assist here. So from there, you know, as I was saying, there's five days left before the window for the public comment closes. So keep posting your stories on Facebook as well as Twitter. And please, please go to the websites of Apco and Nina to provide them with the data that they need to send off to the OMB for reclassification. Now, with that said, today I have a special guest and I want to thank her so much for coming out of the podcast. This is going to be awesome. Today's guest is a former public safety telecommuticator and she is currently the US representative for California's 35th District, Congresswoman Norma Torres. How's it going?",
