    "turn_text": "Right. Do you, do you remember the first time you helped to deliver a baby? I mean, you know, those memories when when you're talking, you know, the mother through childbirth, and then you hear the baby's first cries. I mean, that is, you know, those are wonderful experiences, but not when dispatchers, I don't necessarily think that we remember the good stories and the good endings. We tend to focus on, you know, the really bad stuff that happens because we are trying to work through these very traumatic incidents with our callers and trying to reassure them that we are there to help them and that we are sending them help. Although it may seem like help is never coming, you know, we are and we it's a part of our job to keep them on the phone because just like that little girl, you know, you might be the only witness to their crime, you know, to something tragic that might happen to them.",
