    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75275.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "You know, it's my, my staff is laughing because Whenever people ask me to tell them a 911 story, I always respond by saying, do you want to hear a funny story? Do you want to hear a sad story? Or do you want to hear a sexy story? I've heard it all. And raising my children, you know, I would always refer back and say, There is absolutely nothing that you can say to me that I have not heard before. And, you know, dealing with us, our families and our spouses, this job really hardens us. I remember when, you know, a time when my husband was a victim of a robbery and he was robbed at gunpoint and he called the house to tell me that, you know, he had been robbed, his wallet and, you know, everything was stolen. And, but he was okay. So in my mind, you know, when I listen, you know, to his message, you know, he was okay. So I went about my business like nothing had happened.",
