    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75275.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "He expected a different reaction from his wife. And when he saw me later that day, he was so upset with me because he thought, look, I am not just a caller on the other side of the phone and your spouse, you're supposed to care about what happens to me. And I, you know, try to reassure him. I do care about you, but I don't know. The only way that I could deal with that stressful situation that you were in was by putting myself back at the 911 center and thinking and in hearing that you were okay and everything else, you know, could be replaced as long as you're okay. So those are the types of, you know, emotions that people don't realize. We are human beings. and we care about people. And that is why we do this kind of this type of work. But training is necessary and it is so important that we have, you know, the best tools to do our job.",
