    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm right there with you with the midnight shift. I loved midnight shift and people would say, oh, so how's work been going? I say, well, it's sometimes it's kind of boring. And they would say, well, isn't that a good thing? And then I'd say, well, not for me because I want to help. So, you know, the public, they don't always understand it. But, you know, segueing from that now, I mean, this is a perfect segue into One of the main issues, one of the big things going on right now is this reclassification of PSTs or public safety telecommunicators with the OMB or the Office of Management and Budget to be switched from office administrative or clerical to the protective class. This all started out, of course, as you know, with APCO. You know, they started this out. The OMB ended up projecting it. APCO ended up going out to people and saying, you know, we need your data. We need you to share stories. And Nina kind of jumped in there as well, trying to help out for, you know, for this whole effort. And then I came in out of left field with the story piece of this to help tell the stories of dispatchers with the IM 901 movement. So we're all pretty much unified trying to get this reclassification done. But you added a very important piece to this in this fight in the form of a letter that went directly to the OMB. And for those who don't know about the letter that you ended up sending out, if you could give just a short overview of what you had said in it.",
